WEBVTT

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:22.640
Nagisa!

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.040
Leave it to me!

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:34.100
That was great, Nagisa!

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:34.780
You did it!

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:37.810
I'm not done yet.

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.900
What kind of experiment are 
you doing this time, Honoka?

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:45.620
If you mix these two liquids 
together, it'll freeze in a second.

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:48.000
I'm going to mix them now.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:55.580
Honoka!

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:00.640
See? It's a success!

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:31.960
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:34.770
<i>Pretty Cure Pretty Cure</i>

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:37.610
<i>Pretty Cure Pretty Cure</i>

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:41.880
<i>We're pretty and cure cure Together we are...</i>

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:44.850
<i>PRETTY CURE...!</i>

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:47.720
<i>Out of the frying pan, into the fire</i>

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:49.620
<i>Frankly, it's totally unbelievable</i>

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:53.520
<i>Even in our school in our 
school uniforms, we're both</i>

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:55.130
<i>amazingly tough</i>

00:01:56.630 --> 00:02:00.930
<i>Each time we get out of a tight spot, we both</i>

00:02:01.570 --> 00:02:03.030
<i>become stronger</i>

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:06.800
<i>and closer</i>

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:10.810
<i>Yeah! Your best! My best! Because we're alive</i>

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:13.380
<i>we never fail!</i>

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:16.550
<i>Don't you know that good fortune 
comes to the gates of laughter?</i>

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:19.420
<i>Out with the negative!</i>

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:25.690
<i>Brighten up your life!
Try with all your might...</i>

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:26.590
<i>Work like the devil!</i>

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:29.290
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:32.100
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.990
<i>We're pretty and cure cure</i>

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:36.570
<i>Together we are</i>

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:39.640
<i>Pretty Cure...!</i>

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:52.320
"YOU WANT US TO TRANSFORM!? NO WAY!"

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:00.990
Verone Academy

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:05.320
Nagisa!

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:07.140
Good morning, Shiho.

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:08.080
Good morning.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:09.500
Good morning, Nagisa.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.450
Good morning, Rina.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.710
Hey! Did you all see the 
shooting stars yesterday?

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:15.770
I did. I did.

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:17.220
It was spectacular, wasn't it?

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:18.350
Was it?

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:21.190
There's been a lot of them lately.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.980
I made lots and lots of wishes.

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:26.450
I didn't see any.

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:30.730
But I heard that shooting stars are ominous 
signs that something bad will happen.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:31.420
Is that so?

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:33.330
That's not true.

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:35.390
Yukishiro-san...

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:39.190
Shooting stars are little 
pieces of stars that

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:41.060
drift through the universe.

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:43.330
They're pulled down by the earth's gravity,

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:47.330
and at about 62 miles in the sky, they 
emit light from atmospheric friction.

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:52.260
When people in the olden 
days saw that strange sight,

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:55.330
they began to make wishes upon them.

00:03:57.390 --> 00:04:02.520
Isn't that better than thinking 
that they bring something bad?

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:05.610
Something good is sure to happen.

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:09.600
I'll see you later.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:12.390
What is she? A walking encyclopedia?

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:16.960
You were in a different 
class in our first year,

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:20.320
don't know her well, but we all called 
Yukishiro-san the "Queen of Knowledge."

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:22.200
"Queen of Knowledge"?

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.810
On top of that...

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:25.600
She's really popular with 
all the boys in school.

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:29.050
Nakajima from the kendo team 
confessed his love to her.

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:32.070
Really? Nakajima's just my type.

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:34.330
That's awesome!

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:36.500
Maybe I should "eat her nail 
clippings" (follow her example).

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:37.960
It's "drink," isn't it?

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:40.510
Is it?

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:44.950
Aren't these love letters?

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:47.240
You're popular, too, Nagisa.

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:56.430
But... But... They're all from girls.

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:58.250
I have to hand it to you, Nagisa. 
You're so popular.

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:00.570
Oh, be quiet!

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:04.200
Misumi! Nagisa Misumi!

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:07.030
Nagisa!

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:08.180
Yes?

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:11.150
Solve this problem.

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:15.890
You've got to be kidding!

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:18.120
What's wrong, Misumi?

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:20.860
You're in the 8th grade now, 
so this should be easy.

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:23.800
But this is so sudden!

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:27.140
Mr. Miyashita! She can't solve that problem.

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:29.100
What, Yukishiro-san?

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:31.790
Are you saying Misumi's not smart 
enough to solve this problem?

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:33.870
That hurts! But he's right.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:35.960
That's not what I meant.

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:40.360
It's going to come out to zero equals 
twenty-six, which is a strange answer.

00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:41.330
What?

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:44.180
She's right!

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:50.190
Shouldn't 19 plus X be 19 minus X?

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:54.780
In that case, the answer 
would be X equals 13.

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:58.670
You're right. I'll be more careful next time.

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:06.860
Yukishiro-san!

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:07.970
Yes?

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:11.790
Thank you for what you did earlier.

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:14.360
Not at all.

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:26.190
That's right I just had a great idea.

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:27.260
What? What is it?

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:29.330
When we decide on the next class officer,

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:31.950
how about letting Nagisa 
and Yukishiro-san do it?

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:34.030
That's a good idea!

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:36.000
You're talking about combining 
Yukishiro-san, who's popular with the boys,

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.600
together with Nagisa, who's
 popular with the girls, aren't you?

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:39.830
Isn't it a good idea?

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:41.940
No way! That's not my thing.

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:44.770
I think it's a good idea.

00:06:57.640 --> 00:06:59.060
I'm home!

00:06:59.060 --> 00:06:59.860
Welcome back.

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:13.740
What good is it to only 
be popular with the girls?

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:17.080
I'd like to be popular with boys sometimes.

00:07:32.860 --> 00:07:35.020
Shooting stars?

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:38.820
I'd better make a wish!

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:41.210
I wish I could find a wonderful boyfriend.

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:42.560
I wish I had slim legs.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:44.630
I wish I could buy a lot of clothes.

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:47.010
I wish i could eat my fill of chocolate cake.

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:51.440
That can't be!

00:08:17.270 --> 00:08:20.970
Wha... what is this?

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:26.440
Chutaro?

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:32.150
What's wrong, Chutaro?

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:36.420
Chutaro?

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:38.010
What is it?

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:44.030
Chutaro!

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:47.670
Is that you Honoka?

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:50.130
I'm home, Grandmother.

00:08:50.510 --> 00:08:52.790
Is something wrong with Chutaro?

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:55.110
No... I think he's okay.

00:08:57.010 --> 00:08:59.250
Is there something here?

00:09:12.970 --> 00:09:13.880
This?

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:23.990
What is this?

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:40.620
Mepo!

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:46.990
Who are you mepo?

00:09:46.990 --> 00:09:49.340
It talks...

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:52.070
And in Japanese, too.

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:54.000
Are you a girl mepo?

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:56.340
Stay away from me!

00:09:56.590 --> 00:09:58.270
Take care of me mepo.

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:03.660
Ryota! I wonder what all that racket is.

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:05.000
Go and take a look.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.610
Just leave her alone.

00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:08.810
Never mind! Just do as I say.

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:15.990
Sis! Mom wants to know what's going on.

00:10:18.730 --> 00:10:19.670
What is it?

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:21.410
Listen, Ryota...

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:23.470
What I'm about to show you isn't a dream.

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:25.630
It's real. Stay calm, and look at it.

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:28.600
You're the one who needs to calm down.

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:31.380
Actually, there's something strange in here.

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:31.910
Over there.

00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:35.450
That's not fair, Sis! 
You bought a cell phone.

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:37.590
A cell phone? No, it's not!

00:10:37.590 --> 00:10:39.520
There's something strange inside that thing.

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:40.500
In here?

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:42.420
Don't! He might bite you!

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:46.390
I don't hear anything. What is this anyway?

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:49.010
That's strange.

00:10:49.010 --> 00:10:51.860
I'm sure he was talking to me earlier.

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:54.050
Maybe you fell asleep.

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:55.320
Even though it's still early evening.

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:56.270
That does it!

00:10:57.880 --> 00:10:59.830
Be careful, Ryota.

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:04.320
Mom! Nagisa is picking on me again!

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:04.800
Don't tattle!

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:10.230
Did I have these before?

00:11:12.430 --> 00:11:14.940
What are these cards?

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:22.880
It's walking.

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:25.130
What's wrong?

00:11:27.930 --> 00:11:30.770
It's hard walking by myself mepo.

00:11:30.770 --> 00:11:32.050
Hey, you over there...

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:35.100
Take me to Mipple, my Princess of Hope mepo.

00:11:35.330 --> 00:11:37.210
What are you talking about?

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:37.910
I'm not taking you.

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:40.050
Please mepo.

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:42.360
I don't have anyone else I can rely on mepo.

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:45.510
I know, but...

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:01.720
By the way...

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:03.970
Why the net mepo?

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:06.060
Don't complain.

00:12:06.060 --> 00:12:07.760
Turn right mepo.

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:08.910
Yeah, yeah...

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:10.390
No... Turn left mepo.

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:11.540
I mean go straight mepo.

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:14.260
I've had enough of your "mepo mepo."

00:12:14.260 --> 00:12:15.510
Straight ahead is a dead end.

00:12:15.740 --> 00:12:18.530
Never mind. Just keep on 
going straight ahead mepo.

00:12:18.530 --> 00:12:20.250
How am I supposed to do that?

00:12:21.270 --> 00:12:22.720
Please mepo!

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:25.550
Trying to get me with your tears again?

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:33.290
Who are you anyway?

00:12:33.950 --> 00:12:37.830
I'm the Chosen Guardian from the 
Field of Light, Mepple mepo.

00:12:37.830 --> 00:12:41.420
Field of Light? Guardian? You?

00:12:45.100 --> 00:12:46.610
You don't look it.

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:49.840
Keep going straight mepo.

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:58.490
I must protect the Field of Light from 
the evil forces from Dotsuku Zone mepo.

00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:01.880
I'm so hungry!

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:04.030
Listen to me mepo!

00:13:05.490 --> 00:13:07.000
Hurry mepo!

00:13:07.820 --> 00:13:09.720
This looks like the end.

00:13:10.030 --> 00:13:12.750
But I'm sure it's in this direction mepo.

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:16.110
Something's wrong mepo.

00:13:16.110 --> 00:13:18.660
I can feel something besides Mipple mepo.

00:13:18.660 --> 00:13:19.810
What do you mean by "something"?

00:13:20.380 --> 00:13:23.190
This is the end of the line, young lady.

00:13:28.180 --> 00:13:29.740
I've been looking for you.

00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:31.440
Who are you?

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:33.610
My name is Pisard.

00:13:34.460 --> 00:13:36.430
I came for him.

00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:37.920
Run away mepo!

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:39.400
Sounds like a good idea.

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:44.600
Don't give me a hard time.

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:45.730
Wait a minute.

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:51.760
I'm dizzy mepo!

00:13:54.610 --> 00:13:55.850
Where are the stones?

00:13:56.160 --> 00:13:57.050
Misumi-san!

00:13:58.260 --> 00:13:59.550
Yukishiro-san?

00:13:59.950 --> 00:14:01.050
Mepple!

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:02.080
Mipple!

00:14:02.430 --> 00:14:04.900
What's going on anyway, Yukishiro-san?

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:07.490
She brought me here.

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:08.340
You, too?

00:14:08.340 --> 00:14:10.360
Get Mepple back mipo.

00:14:12.110 --> 00:14:15.170
Well, well... If it isn't the other half...?

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:17.540
Saves me the trouble of looking for you.

00:14:18.070 --> 00:14:20.000
Hand her over.

00:14:20.970 --> 00:14:23.310
No, Honoka! You mustn't 
turn me over to him mipo!

00:14:24.850 --> 00:14:27.140
I'm getting dizzy again mepo!

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:34.420
Thank you mepo.

00:14:36.150 --> 00:14:38.180
No more games!

00:14:43.990 --> 00:14:46.660
That's impossible!

00:14:51.940 --> 00:14:53.630
I can't do this anymore!

00:14:53.630 --> 00:14:54.760
Help me!

00:14:55.090 --> 00:14:56.980
Transform, both of you mepo!

00:14:57.600 --> 00:14:58.430
Transform?

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:00.920
That's not funny!

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:03.380
Take out the Pretty Cure cards mepo.

00:15:04.180 --> 00:15:04.840
Cards?

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:07.450
What are these cards?

00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:09.930
You mean these?

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:11.920
There are a number of cards here.

00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:13.890
Find the Queen card mipo!

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:15.130
I found it.

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:18.050
What do I do with this card?

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:20.520
Swipe the card here mepo!

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:21.970
Like this?

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:23.730
Hurry, you too!

00:15:24.030 --> 00:15:25.060
Is this okay?

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:40.110
Dual Aurora Wave!

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:43.100
What am I saying anyway?

00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:51.640
What happened?

00:17:03.990 --> 00:17:06.310
Protector of the Light, Cure Black!

00:17:06.730 --> 00:17:09.230
Protector of the Light, Cure White!

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:14.740
Together, we are Pretty Cure.

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:19.120
Servants of the power of darkness...

00:17:20.410 --> 00:17:22.630
Go back to where you came from!

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:25.680
What am I saying?

00:17:26.510 --> 00:17:27.790
Quiet!

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:35.960
What?

00:17:36.140 --> 00:17:38.390
Wow! I flew all the way up here!

00:17:38.390 --> 00:17:39.840
How did this happen?

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:42.060
That's the power of Pretty Cure mepo.

00:17:42.060 --> 00:17:43.700
He's coming from above mipo.

00:18:09.200 --> 00:18:10.220
I'm okay.

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:25.040
Damn! You annoying little brats!

00:18:29.810 --> 00:18:33.010
Unleash your anger, Zakenna!

00:18:33.010 --> 00:18:34.330
And with your sinister heart,

00:18:34.330 --> 00:18:36.500
show them how terrifying the 
power of darkness can be!

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:41.330
What is it?

00:18:47.280 --> 00:18:50.300
Zakenna!

00:19:03.880 --> 00:19:06.870
Zakenna!

00:19:07.930 --> 00:19:09.500
This is a joke, isn't it?

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:11.090
Are we dreaming?

00:19:16.790 --> 00:19:18.000
Is this for real?

00:19:24.020 --> 00:19:25.430
That was good, Zakenna!

00:19:28.540 --> 00:19:29.820
He's coming at us mepo!

00:19:29.820 --> 00:19:31.010
Run away mipo!

00:19:35.990 --> 00:19:37.790
Zakenna!

00:19:45.260 --> 00:19:46.990
White is in danger mepo.

00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:51.960
Are you okay?

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:53.270
Thanks.

00:19:56.440 --> 00:19:58.040
This doesn't look good.

00:19:58.360 --> 00:20:00.010
Join hands mepo.

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:02.240
At a time like this?

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:04.210
Just hurry, and do it mipo!

00:20:09.050 --> 00:20:11.290
Black Thunder!

00:20:11.290 --> 00:20:13.080
White Thunder!

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:29.930
The beautiful souls of Pretty Cure...!

00:20:30.440 --> 00:20:33.310
...will crush the sinister hearts!

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:38.050
Pretty Cure Marble Screw!

00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:50.390
What's happening?

00:20:52.950 --> 00:20:55.050
Zakenna!

00:20:56.430 --> 00:21:02.410
Gomenna! Gomenna! Gomenna!

00:20:57.900 --> 00:20:59.260
What is this?

00:21:03.740 --> 00:21:05.370
It's over, isn't it?

00:21:06.340 --> 00:21:08.030
So it seems.

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:09.910
What happened to that strange person?

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:11.070
I have no idea.

00:21:13.470 --> 00:21:15.120
What's going on?

00:21:15.440 --> 00:21:17.040
Who are those two anyway?

00:21:23.570 --> 00:21:25.570
I wonder what's going on?

